514	270,480,922,1475 - 270,1165,380,1475 - 380,1200,440,1475 - 405,1300,550,1475 - 870,1130,922,1300	514. Plant of Crested Dwarf Iris.	The whole plant: narrow sword-shaped leaves from a short creeping rootstock with fibrous roots, and a stem bearing one iris flower with spreading, crested outer divisions.
515	105,1160,445,1475 - 380,1140,445,1195 - 405,1300,445,1475 - 432,1160,445,1215	515. Top of the style and the 3 petal-like stigmas, also 2 of the stamens.	The style dividing at its top into three broad, arching petal-like stigmas, with a slender stamen lying under two of them.
516	875,455,1215,1475 - 875,455,902,1130 - 875,1300,928,1475	516. Magnified pistil and lower part of the tube of the perianth, divided lengthwise: the foliage cut away.	A long slender tube of the perianth rising from an oval ovary cut lengthwise to show its rows of ovules, set between the cut-off bases of two leaves.
517	405,1305,542,1475	517. Lower part of a pod, divided crosswise.	A rounded pod on a short stalk, cut across to show three cells with their seeds.
